## Phase 3: The "Glass" Touch Bypass (Event Delegation)

### Current Architecture

```
User Touch → Flutter Gesture Arena → HtmlElementView → Browser DOM → MapLibre JS
                    ~50-100ms latency added here
```

### Problem Analysis

Flutter Web uses `CanvasKit` rendering which overlays an HTML5 Canvas on top of the MapLibre `<div>`. The `HtmlElementView` widget creates a "slot" in the Flutter canvas, but Flutter's gesture arena still intercepts and re-dispatches touch events. This adds 50-100ms of latency to every pan/zoom gesture.

### Proposed Solution: Selective Pointer Passthrough

> [!CAUTION]
> We **cannot** use blanket `IgnorePointer` because we still need:
> - `onMapClick` for POI selection and pin drops
> - `onMapLongPress` for quick-routing
> - `onCameraMove` / `onCameraIdle` for scale bar and tracking updates
>
> These are **callback-based** (MapLibre fires them to Dart), not **gesture-based** (Dart intercepting DOM events). So they will continue to work even with pointer passthrough.

### Implementation Strategy

```dart
// In full_screen_map.dart, the existing Listener wrapper:
// Current (line 579):
child: Listener(
  behavior: HitTestBehavior.translucent,
  onPointerDown: (PointerDownEvent event) { ... },
  child: MapLibreMap(...)
)

// Proposed:
// 1. Remove the Listener wrapper entirely
// 2. Let MapLibre's own JS event handlers manage touch natively
// 3. Use a CSS override to ensure the Flutter overlay canvas does NOT intercept
```

### CSS Injection (web/index.html)

```css
/* Allow touch events to pass directly to the MapLibre canvas */
flt-glass-pane {
  pointer-events: none !important;
}

/* But re-enable pointer events on the MapLibre container itself */
.maplibregl-canvas-container {
  pointer-events: auto !important;
}

/* And on Flutter overlay elements (sheets, buttons, etc.) */
.flt-platform-view-slot ~ * {
  pointer-events: auto !important;
}
```

### Risk Assessment

> [!WARNING]
> This is the **highest-risk phase**. Blanket `pointer-events: none` on `flt-glass-pane` will break ALL Flutter touch interactions (buttons, sheets, scrolling). The CSS selectors must be surgically scoped to ONLY the map viewport area.
>
> **Recommendation**: Defer this phase until Phases 1 & 2 are validated. The performance gain here (~50ms per gesture) is less impactful than the ~93ms saved in Phases 1+2, and carries significantly more regression risk.

### Safer Alternative: `PointerInterceptor` Pattern

Instead of CSS hacking, use the [`pointer_interceptor`](https://pub.dev/packages/pointer_interceptor) package (officially maintained by Flutter team) which creates a transparent HTML overlay that properly delegates events:

```dart
// Wrap the MapLibreMap in a HitTestBehavior.translucent container
// and wrap all OVERLAY widgets (buttons, sheets) in PointerInterceptor
import 'package:pointer_interceptor/pointer_interceptor.dart';

// For the floating buttons:
PointerInterceptor(
  child: MapControlsPill(...)
)
```

