## Implementation Priority & Risk Matrix

| Phase | Impact | Risk | Effort | Priority |
|-------|--------|------|--------|----------|
| **🔴 Immediate: Kill debugPrint spam** | Critical | None | 1 min | **Done ✅** |
| **Phase 4: RepaintBoundary Isolation** | High | Low | 2 hrs | **P0** |
| **Phase 1: Binary Data Pipeline** | High | Medium | 4 hrs | **P1** |
| **Phase 2: Web Worker Routing** | Very High | Medium | 8 hrs | **P1** |
| **Phase 3: Glass Touch Bypass** | Medium | High | 6 hrs | **P2** |

> [!NOTE]
> **Recommended execution order**: Phase 4 → Phase 1 → Phase 2 → Phase 3.
> Phase 4 is the safest and gives the most immediate UI stability.
> Phase 1 + 2 together eliminate ~95% of the bridge serialization cost.
> Phase 3 should only be attempted after confirming the `pointer_interceptor` pattern works cleanly.

